# Deny-list format. The real file is .denylist (ignored by Git, never committed).
# In CI the same content lives in the DENYLIST_B64 repository secret, as ONE base64 line
# (GitHub masks multi-line secrets line by line, which would reveal terms in the logs):
#   base64 -w0 .denylist | gh secret set DENYLIST_B64
# One term per line. Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
# Matching is case-insensitive and whole-word.
example-term-one
example term two
